<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">League of Nations</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The League of Nations was the international organisation founded after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> to preserve peace and settle disputes. It placed the former colonies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> and Ottoman territories under the mandate system, much of it administered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>. It condemned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> in 1935, but its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">sanctions</a> failed to stop the expansion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/league-of-nations.jpg" alt="League of Nations" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin Grandjean This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape . · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_League_of_Nations_(1939).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
